 % \hyun{Each item hides a single key--value needle at a random depth of a haystack and asks the model to reproduce the value verbatim: S-NIAH-1 hides a numeric value in a repeated-noise haystack, whereas S-NIAH-2 and S-NIAH-3 hide a $7$-digit key and a UUID in natural DCLM text, with $50$ items per context length. The single-key template of \citet{hsieh2024ruler} separates the query from its value with a colon, which subword tokenizers absorb into a single unit but byte-level models do not; we therefore score a colon-free variant of the template for every model, and Appendix~\ref{app:protocol} details this boundary-consistent format and quantifies the artifact it removes.} 
 \hyun{To assess computational efficiency, we measure prefill latency per KiB of text and decode latency per generated byte, with each model at its fastest available setting (Appendix~\ref{app:efficiency}).}
 
