-\hyun{LAMBADA~\citep{lambada} asks for the last word of a narrative passage, a word that is meant to be predictable only from the wider context. We use the OpenAI detokenized version of its test split ($5{,}153$ passages; \texttt{lambada\_openai} in the LM Evaluation Harness~\citep{eval_harness}), zero-shot and without a prompt template. As in the harness, the context is the passage up to its last space, and the target is that space followed by the final word ($6.7$ bytes on average). An item is correct only if the whole target is reproduced under the exact-match criterion above, which is the harness's \texttt{acc} metric. Since the target is a fixed string, every model is asked to produce the same word, whether that word is one or a few subword tokens for the Transformer or a sequence of bytes for the byte-level models. We do not report LAMBADA perplexity, which is normalized per token and therefore not comparable across tokenizations. Each model is scored with the same harness as its downstream tasks (BLT at batch size $1$ for both thresholds), in a run that contains LAMBADA alone, and the $\pm$ in Table~\ref{tab:main_robust} follows the paired bootstrap described below.}
